[32m+[m[32m## Routing Architecture[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Public routes**: `/`, `/features`, `/pricing`, `/benefits`, `/testimonials`, `/contact`, `/privacy-policy`, `/terms-of-service`[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Auth routes**: `/login`, `/signup`[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Dashboard routes** (grouped under `(dashboard)/`): require authentication[m
[32m+[m[32m- **Onboarding routes** (grouped under `(onboarding)/`): post-signup setup[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Data Flow[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m[32mUser → Browser → Next.js Server → API Routes / Firebase Client SDK[m
[32m+[m[32m                                        ↓[m
[32m+[m[32m                              Firestore Database[m
[32m+[m[32m                                        ↓[m
[32m+[m[32m                              Firebase Admin SDK (server-side only)[m
[32m+[m[32m```[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### Auth Flow[m
[32m+[m[32m1. User logs in via Firebase Auth (email/password or Google)[m
[32m+[m[32m2. `onAuthStateChanged` listener in `AuthProvider` updates context[m
[32m+[m[32m3. `AuthProvider` fetches user profile from Firestore `users/{uid}`[m
[32m+[m[32m4. Session cookie set for middleware-aware protection[m
[32m+[m[32m5. Server API routes use `requireRole` middleware with `firebase-admin` ID token verification[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### AI Flow[m
[32m+[m[32m1. User submits prompt from AI Assistant UI[m
[32m+[m[32m2. POST to `/api/ai` with `{ prompt, messages }`[m
[32m+[m[32m3. Server iterates through configured AI providers (OpenRouter / OpenCode)[m
[32m+[m[32m4. Returns first successful response or error[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m## Key Design Decisions[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 1. Role-Based Access Control[m
[32m+[m[32m- 5 roles: `super_admin`, `admin`, `editor`, `finance`, `viewer`[m
[32m+[m[32m- `ROLE_HIERARCHY` numeric levels for minimum-role checks[m
[32m+[m[32m- `PAGE_PERMISSIONS` dictionary for CRUD-level access per page[m
[32m+[m[32m- Enforced both client-side (UI hiding) and server-side (`requireRole`)[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 2. Multi-Tenancy via churchId[m
[32m+[m[32m- Every document includes a `churchId` field[m
[32m+[m[32m- Firestore security rules enforce per-church access isolation[m
[32m+[m[32m- `churchId` defaults to the user's UID on first signup[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 3. i18n[m
[32m+[m[32m- 4 languages: English, French, Spanish, Portuguese[m
[32m+[m[32m- Language detection via browser navigator.language[m
[32m+[m[32m- Persisted via i18next-browser-languagedetector[m
[32m+[m
[32m+[m[32m### 4. Demo Mode[m
[32m+[m[32m- Creates a temporary Firebase account with random email[m
[32m+[m[32m- Seeds 12 data collections with realistic sample data[m
[32m+[m[32m- One-click "Try Demo" button on signup page[m
[32m+[m
